  "html_content": "Subject: City Council Meeting \n\n# \u2709\ufe0f City Council Meeting\n*Your quick guide to what's on the City Council Meeting agenda \u2014 September 29, 2025*\n\n## \ud83d\udde3\ufe0f How to Participate\n- **Meeting:** [Monday, September 29 at 4:30 PM](https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&text=City%20Council%20Meeting&dates=20250929T233000Z/20250930T013000Z&location=Redwood%20Room%2C%202180%20Milvia%20Street%2C%206th%20Floor%2C%20Berkeley%2C%20CA%2094704%20%26%20Virtual&details=Regular%20meeting%20to%20discuss%20city%20governance%20and%20community%20issues.) \ud83d\udcc5\n- **Where:** Redwood Room, 2180 Milvia Street, 6th Floor, Berkeley, CA 94704 & Virtual\n- **Watch Online:** Not specified.\n- **Call In:** Not specified.\n- **Email Comments:** council@cityofberkeley.info \u2014 **deadline:** Not specified.\n- **Attend & Speak:** Check meeting agenda for public comment rules\n- **Full Agenda:** [View original meeting agenda](https://berkeleyca.gov/community-recreation/events?field_event_category_tid=104)\n\n## \ud83d\udea8 What's on the Agenda\n### City Council Meeting\n- **Change:** Regular meeting to discuss city governance and community issues.\n- **Impact:** Decisions made can affect local policies, budgets, and community projects. Cost not specified.\n- **Action:** Attend in person or virtually via Zoom. Public comments can be made by raising hand in Zoom or submitting a speaker card in person.\n\n## \u2705 Bottom Line\nFound 6 civic meeting opportunities in Berkeley's calendar.\n\n\u26a1 *Independent and nonpartisan summary. Facts only; no spin.*",
